                <pb facs="0147" n="45" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg45"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.79614/1: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Guatemala</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Geissler</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-02-03T12:00:00-07:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 3,
                                1927—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 7:50 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>21. Referring to the Department’s telegram of February 1, 5 p.m. Parada went to
                    San Salvador 10 days ago. It is thought here that he is backed by the Mexican
                    Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Geissler</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
